(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #135: `group`, `my` and `every` are claimed only in
 the shape of a group form, so each still names a pid anywhere else,
 including as the pid of a `Send signal` itself. Signal 0 to a forked
 child only.)

a number called group is 0.
a number called my is 0.
a number called every is 0.
Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Wait 30 seconds.
If pid is greater than 0 then,
    Set group to pid.
    Set my to pid.
    Set every to pid.
    Send signal 0 to process group.
    On error print "unexpected error on group".
    Send signal 0 to my.
    On error print "unexpected error on my".
    Send signal 0 to every.
    On error print "unexpected error on every".
    Print "group, my and every each reached the child".
    Send signal 9 to process pid.
    Set reaped to reap process pid.
    If reaped is pid then,
        Print "the child is stopped and reaped".
